Laya multilingual Android sample

This sample ports the host-side tokenizer, question builder, decoder, and
calibration lookup to Kotlin for LiteRT and provides a Compose/MVVM application.
The host contract and preset schemas follow Laya 0.3.4 by Convai Innovations,
licensed under Apache License 2.0.
https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya
Checkpoint revision: 1c5edc17a7acd8701df6fc341c0d179f1c62c982

Model conversion changes: static windows, explicit attention and rotary-position
operations, separate action head, host-side token embedding lookup, and optional
FP16 storage of fully connected weights. The checkpoint tokenizer and calibration
provenance are retained. The calibration JSON is an external asset; raw source
calibration datasets are not included in this module.

The multilingual encoder derives from mmBERT-base, declared MIT by its model card.
